WEBVTT

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:38.340
Orienteering! They told those of us 
from Class 2-2 to get started!

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.370
What are you so excited about?

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.860
I'm trying to shake off the incompetence!

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:50.430
The only ones who are excited 
for this are you and Kominato.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.080
Let's get out and go!

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.670
Yo, yo, yo!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.390
Super orienteering!

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.840
You'll get sucked into it soon, 
too, Kou! Just you wait!

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.430
We're gonna score 
a lot of them points!

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.430
Sounds like a pain.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.490
Move out!

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.300
Yeah!

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.850
<i>I'm doing my best.</i>

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.160
<i>I'm going to improve our team's vibe!</i>

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.250
<i>So I can unite our feelings.</i>

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.090
<i>I just know something 
will start from there.</i>

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.860
<i>Something new!</i>

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.090
Ah! Found the checkpoint!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:33.880
<b>Checkpoint</b>

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.620
Hey, there you are!

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.880
We're doing a mixed juice guessing game.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.340
There are ten ingredients in all.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.680
For each one you identify, you get one point!

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.330
Apple and banana are definites, right?

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.860
Oh, what else...

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.600
Mabuchi's having a weird reaction.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.060
What's wrong, Kou?

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.300
Tastes like celery.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.570
What, really?

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.200
Hmm...

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.650
I don't know...

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.720
It's definitely in there.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.410
Kou, you don't like celery?

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.360
Let's put some faith in that reaction.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.190
Murao-san, that's not fair! 
Figure it out with us!

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.820
Of course, it's only full of things 
that are safe to drink, right?

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.390
Of course! I made it myself.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:38.940
Thyme.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.760
What? You want a time-out?

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.700
No. There's thyme in it.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.910
Thyme?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.910
Oh! Thyme the herb?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.780
Amazing! You're the first team 
that's guessed celery and thyme!

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.170
You've got the highest score yet!

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:02.050
<b>the</b>

00:03:58.910 --> 00:03:59.530
Here!

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.050
It's your point card and your first keyword.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.310
Collect them all, okay?

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.010
Okay!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.550
Hey.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:09.800
You starting to want to 
try to win with our team?

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:10.850
I sure am!

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.690
<i>But are the others into it?</i>

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.100
It's hot out here.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.650
<b>They seem kind of into it</b>

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.650
I'll do my best!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:23.610
<i>I feel like our feelings are 
united for the first time!</i>

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.450
Okay! Let's get this going!

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.080
Wait! Wait!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.680
We should look at the map.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.840
Yoshioka, consider the meaning 
of the smiles on that team.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:36.460
Huh?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.920
You're such a genius!

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:42.010
<b>Members of another team</b>

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.410
Let's keep it going!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.010
Those smiles will lead us to the checkpoint!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.880
Go, go, go!

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.390
W-Wait, everyone! Let's check the map!

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.310
<b>Orienteering Point Check Stamp Sheet</b>

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.310
<b>clear                  clear                  clear</b>

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.310
<b>the       in</b>

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.880
I've got a feeling the next one is that way!

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.680
But let's look at the map!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.060
<b>in       the       the</b>

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.350
This way!

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.270
Wait! The map!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.020
<b>in       the       the       area</b>

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:00.860
<b>in       the       the
area       lake</b>

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.140
This way!

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.320
The map...

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.540
Is that the last checkpoint?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.750
Yeah. We're finally here.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.250
<i>I feel like I haven't contributed anything.</i>

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:29.100
You didn't tell Yoshioka-san what 
you saw during cleaning time?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.660
Would it have been okay to tell her?

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.330
I didn't tell her anything. Don't worry.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:41.650
I think it would be okay 
to tell Futaba-chan, but...

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.610
What is it? What are we talking about?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.590
It's nothing, Futaba-chan!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.660
I see!

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:59.420
<i>I guess I shouldn't pry any further, then.</i>

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.110
<i>I keep getting cut off from 
the things I want to say.</i>

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.770
<i>But this is no time to get all depressed!</i>

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.130
<i>The reason I'm working hard 
right now is to change that.</i>

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:11.890
<i>Next! Next!</i>

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.850
Okay! We got all the keywords!

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.810
Um, we're supposed to line them up, right?

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.270
<b>in       the       the
area       lake       biggest</b>

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:24.270
"The biggest lake in the area"?

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:27.740
Oh, that must be the finish line!

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.660
Here it is!

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.490
We've got good points, 
and our time is really great.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.980
I think we could seriously...

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.620
<b>Win!</b>

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.120
Let's go!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.250
Um, where are we?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.070
We've just been running around 
randomly all this time,

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.220
so I don't know our current location.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.860
I know! We could use an app 
on our smartphones!

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.630
We left those with the teachers.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.440
What should we do?

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:02.940
No problem!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.560
In terrain like this, you look 
at the shape of the mountains,

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:09.990
the location of the sun, 
and work it out from there!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.730
We're lost. Completely.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.720
This sucks.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.390
What, are you saying this is my fault?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.060
I wasn't saying that.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.730
You all went along with me!

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.230
I said I wasn't saying that!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.540
This is no time to argue!

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.690
We just have to get out of these woods!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:51.550
The woods aren't that big.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.140
If we just keep walking, 
we'll find a way out eventually.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.570
But...

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:58.880
Is it okay to just walk around randomly?

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.130
Don't you think

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:04.040
it would be better to wait here 
until the teachers come to find us?

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.900
I hear a river.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:18.140
If the finish line is on the 
other side of the river,

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.770
the way out should be 
in that direction, too.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.820
Let's just get as far as we 
can while the sun's out.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:26.620
And, if it gets totally dark,

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.220
we'll do what Makita suggested 
and stay wherever we are.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.150
How does that sound?

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.470
It's okay. We're all here with you!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.580
Hey, there it is! The river!

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.930
The current doesn't seem 
very fast. It's safe.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:47.790
Let's go.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:48.750
Sure!

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.050
Easy, easy!

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.280
Don't relax until it's finished.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.510
That scared me!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.030
Yuuri, be careful!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.610
I'm scared! I can't do it!

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:21.660
Don't be scared! Go rock by rock!

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.640
Just jump!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.100
Calm down! You can do it!

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.120
Don't say it all at once!

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.120
Don't worry.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:28.330
What is she doing?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:30.580
Makita!

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.640
Here. Take my hand.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.470
But I'm scared!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.460
It's fine! Come here!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.220
C'mon.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:42.650
I'm gonna fall! I'm gonna fall! I'm scared!

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.600
But you did it.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.590
Let's keep going, just like that.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.070
Okay?

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.350
Sure.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.950
Makita! Do your best!

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:11.260
<i>Kou... he really is amazing. He 
completely calmed Yuuri down.</i>

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.300
Look at that, you did great!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.780
Thank you, Mabuchi-kun.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.080
Sure.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.270
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.770
No, I'm glad you're okay!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.810
Okay, let's go.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.770
We'd better pick up the pace a little.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:44.070
<i>This is bad. The foot I fell on earlier... 
it really hurts to walk on it!</i>

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.970
Does your foot hurt?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.970
Oh, no, not at all!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.240
It does, doesn't it?

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:09.340
From before?

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.140
Futaba-chan...

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:15.650
I'll find the way out and 
have a teacher come for us.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:20.800
It'll be dark soon. It's dangerous 
to keep going like this.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.910
It would be more worse
 for us to split up.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:27.470
If it gets dark before you find the way out,
 that would be more dangerous.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.020
I can take it! Let's just keep walking!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.510
Kominato, take this.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:40.460
Here.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.980
I'll carry you. Get on.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.530
What?! No!

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:47.760
That's embarrassing!

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.600
I don't care about your sense of modesty.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.100
Just get on, if you don't 
want to slow everyone down.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:01.570
Futaba-chan. I'll take your bag.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:03.490
Sure.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:07.820
Well... if you insist, then.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:11.870
I'm heavy.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.210
It's fine. Get on.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:14.550
Okay.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.590
Wow. More than I thought...

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.420
I-I really will weigh you down! 
I-I'll walk, after all!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:26.220
It's fine. If you weigh me down, 
it just reminds me that you're there.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.180
That's a weird reassurance...

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.920
<i>But... it's like he's saying 
he wants me to be here.</i>

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.520
<i>Not a bad feeling, right?</i>

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.370
<i>It's weird...</i>

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.030
<i>So warm...</i>

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.910
<i>Smells like Kou...</i>

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.000
Yuuri...

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.590
You still awake?

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.760
Yeah, I'm awake.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.850
Today got complicated, 
but it was fun, wasn't it?

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:50.680
Yeah. Though we came in 
dead last in the end.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:53.990
Listen...

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:58.220
...during the orienteering...

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.430
You and Murao-san...

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:06.570
Never mind.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.180
Futaba-chan. I...

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:17.830
I've been by myself for a long time, 
but that doesn't mean I wasn't lonely.

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:25.630
When you talked to me the first time, 
do you know how happy it made me?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.030
That's why...

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:35.810
I'll never leave you 
by yourself, Futaba-chan.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:44.690
M-Me either! Because I know what it 
feels like to be all by yourself!

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:52.620
So I'll stay with you, too, Yuuri.
 No matter what happens.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:54.940
Okay!

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:21.490
Kou...?

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:27.030
Kou!

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.080
Yoshioka.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.030
What are you doing up at this hour?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:36.030
I happened to wake up. 
I thought I'd watch the sunrise.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:39.720
Is your foot okay?

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.830
It's fine now. The medicine worked.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.410
I see.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:51.400
The sky's getting lighter. 
You can't tell if it's night or day.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:56.630
This sky's a little like you, Kou.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.100
In what way?

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:01.590
I can't tell if you're nice or not.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.450
That's just like you, too, then.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.190
Huh?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.390
I can't tell if you're 
incompetent or capable.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.330
<i>The time between night and day...</i>

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:20.600
<i>That's what we are.</i>

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:30.060
It's chilly out here. Put it on.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.260
But won't you be cold, Kou?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.710
Just do it.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:37.840
Thanks.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.410
It's still a little while longer before sunrise.

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:43.260
I know!

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:54.070
You got the jump on me!

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.240
You...

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.800
You went back to the room, 
but didn't get yourself a jacket?

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.420
Oh, that's right! 
Sorry, I'll give back your parka.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:08.590
It's fine.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.410
Keep it on.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:37.570
And... it's coming! It's coming!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.690
It's here!

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.230
The night has ended.

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.310
It's the start of a new day!

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:53.930
<i>The smell of wet earth.</i>

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:55.970
<i>The smell of dewy grass.</i>

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.530
<i>The smell of morning in May.</i>

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:03.450
<i>I don't think I'll ever forget 
watching the sunrise</i>

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:06.080
<i>with everyone like this!</i>

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:09.390
So that someday, when you look back,

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.890
the people you experienced it with 
will see it as a "happy memory"

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:17.010
with the same warmth that you do.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.240
I liked that thing you said. 
Feels like "being young."

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:24.690
You're embarrassing me.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.470
You shy about that kind of thing?

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:36.560
People should save the stoic act
 for when they get all old!

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:39.400
I don't think you'll ever change, 
even when you do grow old.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:56.780
Anyone forget anything? No one? 
We're moving out!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.270
<i>Heavy!</i>

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.580
Shuuei Line - Sakigatani Station

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.550
Yeah. Sure, thanks.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.760
Mom said she'd pick me up.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:20.790
I see.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.140
It really doesn't hurt that much anymore.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.770
Still, it's better not to push it.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.970
Yeah. You're right.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.600
Kou, you're not going home?

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.760
Oh, a cat.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.740
Were you waiting with me?

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.850
I'll be okay. You can go home if you—

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:54.940
Hey, look at this guy! He's got one sock on.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.380
He's still a little one, huh?

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.560
Think he's a stray? He's so tame.

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:14.450
<i>I'm starting to learn things about Kou.</i>

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.520
<i>He hates celery.</i>

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.260
<i>He likes cats.</i>

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:21.240
<i>His teasing is only superficial.</i>

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:25.400
<i>Deep down... he's nice.</i>

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.730
Oh, the car's here.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.030
Then I'll go home, too.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:39.540
Later.

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:43.490
Kou!

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:46.470
Thanks for waiting with me.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.430
I was just playing with the cat.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.550
That's what I thought you'd say!

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.400
<i>He's not the Kou from back then.</i>

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.860
<i>His voice has changed. He's taller.</i>

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.820
<i>But the 16-year-old Kou...</i>

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:06.540
<i>I know him now.</i>

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.790
<i>And what's causing my heart to pound is...</i>

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:18.750
<i>The 16-year-old Kou... I really...</i>

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.680
An e-mail from Yuuri?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:34.640
From: Yuuri 
 Title: All done! 

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:38.430
"I'm not mad at Kominato-kun anymore..."

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:48.030
And... 
 Listen... I... 
 I think I've fallen for 
 Mabuchi-kun!

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:40.980
Next Episode . . .

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:29.220
<i>The reason I think I really like him is...</i>

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:35.360
<i>Because when he helped me cross the 
river in the forest, he was so nice.</i>

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:40.980
<i>He made my heart pound, but... 
he also set me at ease...</i>
